{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787384173921567001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"grateful-electronic-vaquita","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"85ad0d89ac1ea037dadda6160a47e58fe53d6746ebcf5ad82da3b6ff4ea111af","event_uuid":"09f0e516-4749-4fc1-9331-b2726b571b2f","position":{"commit_sha":"67ed022f9ef49b4f2e6dcbbb75dc6ec34f640b1b","position":"1787378985906874001-09f0e516-4749-4fc1-9331-b2726b571b2f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"56c0be061aa631f0a1c5a9d7f5d5fbb23194373eba530360fba158703ad71994","event_uuid":"153f94a1-807e-4bcf-bc56-209c8085a6fc","position":{"commit_sha":"5eef99a869325e24b6cf10f35c946e722a55772a","position":"1787379015542729001-153f94a1-807e-4bcf-bc56-209c8085a6fc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787378985906874001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"153f94a1-807e-4bcf-bc56-209c8085a6fc","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1dd5-1880-17d0-4ac0"}],"description":"`scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py --check-planning-corpus` exits 1 on current `origin/main`:\n\n```\nplanning-corpus check: corpus=114 (want 113); missed=[]; mechanical_fp=[]; FAIL\n```\n\nReproduced UNCHANGED on a pristine detached worktree at `origin/main` (with the tracker symlinked in), so this is not caused by ticket 1dd5's change: the flagged set is still exactly `ADJUDICATED_SUBSTANTIVE` (`missed=[]`, `mechanical_fp=[]`); only the corpus SIZE arm fails.\n\nRoot cause shape: the corpus is described in the module docstring as 'pinned and reproducible', but it is re-derived at run time from LIVE ticket state — the ancestors of `PLANNING_CORPUS_BOUNDARY` whose subject prefix resolves to a ticket whose CURRENT `ticket_type` is `bug` (`_resolve_bug_ticket` -> `_ticket_type`). Reclassifying any historical ticket to/from `bug`, or adding a ticket that changes short-prefix resolution, moves the count. `PLANNING_CORPUS_SIZE = 113` is therefore a constant asserted against a moving derivation.\n\nNothing in CI or the test suite runs this script, so the drift went unnoticed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `python scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py --check-planning-corpus` exits 0 on `origin/main`, OR the size assertion is replaced by one that does not depend on live ticket state (e.g. pin the 113 SHAs, not the count).\n- [ ] The decision is recorded in the script's docstring so the 'pinned and reproducible' claim matches what the code does.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"648b-7882-497f-45fc","ticket_type":"bug","title":"backtest --check-planning-corpus pin drifts: corpus=114, want 113","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["09f0e516-4749-4fc1-9331-b2726b571b2f","153f94a1-807e-4bcf-bc56-209c8085a6fc"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787384173921567001,"uuid":"74b0b3b0-3934-4bd0-b62a-66c6cf6ad5ee"}